# What `vsce package` EXCLUDES from the .vsix (Doc 28 §3-V6 / Doc 27
# §8-V6). The duck-principle bar: a genuinely installable VSIX that is
# lean (no source / no node_modules / no test corpus) yet REAL (the
# esbuild `dist/` runtime bundle AND the bundled `bin/<host-triple>/`
# native binaries that V1's Rule-2 resolver loads ARE shipped).
#
# Anything NOT matched here is included. `dist/**` (the esbuild output,
# the extension `main`) and `bin/**` (the bundled host-triple `fsm` +
# `fsm-lang-server`) are deliberately NOT excluded — they are the
# functional payload. `package.json`, `language-configuration.json`,
# `snippets/`, `syntaxes/`, `assets/`, `README`/`LICENSE`-class metadata
# are kept by vsce by default.

# --- TypeScript sources & build inputs (the runtime is the esbuild
# `dist/` bundle, NOT `src/` — shipping `src/` would bloat the VSIX with
# code the host never loads). ---
src/**
out/**
.vscode-test/**
*.vsix
**/*.ts
**/*.map
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.webview.json
esbuild.mjs
copy-fixtures.mjs
scripts/**

# --- node_modules: the extension is esbuild-bundled (esbuild.mjs bundles
# the language client + deps INTO dist/extension.js), so the VSIX needs
# ZERO runtime node_modules — excluding it is the single biggest size win
# and is correctness-safe here precisely because of the esbuild bundle. ---
node_modules/**

# --- Lint / VCS / editor / CI metadata (never user-facing). ---
.eslintrc*
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
.github/**
**/.DS_Store

# --- Anything that would re-introduce the cargo target trough or test
# fixtures into the package. ---
**/*.rs
**/fixtures/**
